  "proposed_findings": [
    "The ordered-first-mark argument gives an informal direct proof of the registered ordinary-leaf order band, subject to independent controller review; it uses the one-mark-per-component root fact and correct p-1 rank shift.",
    "At |T|=2p+2 the ordered proof has a one-vertex shadow gap. With a nontrivial component root first, only the first degree-one root and a second singleton root can attain the exceptional |J_i|=2k bound.",
    "The p=6 order-14 listed instrument has 240 eligible shell rows among 3159 free tree classes and reports maximum full S=-222; this is bounded computation.",
    "The global lower-region target and first-shell target remain unresolved by this preparation; Cycle 2 allocation prioritizes cross-support compensation and exact full-sum witnesses."
  ],
  "exact_limitations": [
    "No Lean code was built or kernel checked; the ordinary-leaf proof is an independently audited informal proposal, not a formal award.",
    "No proof of the eligible |T|=2p+2 shell or of the complete lower-region favorable-leaf aggregate is supplied.",
    "No eligible ordinary tree with positive complete selected sum is supplied; positive local and support-fibre terms do not refute the primary.",
    "The p=6 instrument was parsed and summarized from a listed source, not independently recomputed; its finite boundary is orders 14 and 15 at p=6.",
    "The Cycle 1 adjudications are proposed summaries; their finite searches and replay dependencies are not universal evidence.",
    "The generic marked-isolate proof was not formalized, and the ordered-mark ordinary-leaf argument does not alone prove its wider graph scope.",
